# Judge credentials. Copy to .env (git-ignored) or export in your shell.
#
# Nothing loads .env automatically. An interactive run reads the environment, and
# the scheduled runs pass it explicitly: `node --env-file=.env bin/webmcp-gauge.mjs`
# (see scripts/spaced-session.cmd). Worth knowing because a scheduled task cannot
# see a key that only exists inside your shell - the first spaced session failed in
# under a second with "No judge API key found" for exactly that reason.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works; the model id is recorded in every report
# because invocation rate is a property of (page, client, judge model).
#
# The frozen Airlock utterance set was authored by "deepseek v4 by agentrouter",
# so that model must not be used as the judge for those numbers - the CLI refuses.

WEBMCP_GAUGE_JUDGE_API_KEY=
WEBMCP_GAUGE_JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://agentrouter.org/v1
WEBMCP_GAUGE_JUDGE_MODEL=glm-5.3

# Chrome. The harness launches its own browser per session by default - a cold
# profile seeded with only the WebMCP flag, in --headless=new - so neither of
# these is required. Set CDP_PORT only to attach to a browser you started
# yourself, which also means sessions share a process and page cache.
# WEBMCP_GAUGE_CHROME=C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe
# CDP_PORT=9333
# WEBMCP_GAUGE_CHROME_LOG=1   # pass Chrome's own stderr through, for launch debugging
